# NestedText v3 - dita.v1_3 specializations DETAIL pass (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/org.oasis-open.dita.v1_3/dtd/ (script census).
# Last of the what-is-not-yet-transmigrated remainder.

specialization-census:
    technicalContent: 82 files, 952.7 KB, largest specialization in the corpus
    learning: 41 files, 344.7 KB
    base: 25 files, 264.8 KB
    subjectScheme: 7 files, 77.3 KB
    bookmap: 4 files, 62.0 KB
    machineryIndustry: 3 files, 14.5 KB
    xnal: 3 files, 23.2 KB

specialize-never-edit:
    > technicalContent's 82 files narrow base's 25 without touching them:
    > constraint modules redeclare parameter entities before the base
    > loads, so the base file is never opened for editing. bookmap's 4
    > files organize whole books; subjectScheme's 7 bind attribute values
    > to taxonomies; learning's 41 carry pedagogy. Each specialization is
    > additive law over an untouched base.

release-binding:
    > Stream 18 (per-command laws abolished): specialization is the named
    > precedent, a command constrains a subset's law without editing the
    > subset, the way technicalContent constrains topic. Stream 9
    > (convergence): the 82-file specialization is the largest single
    > convergence input; converge the constraints, never the base.
